#. macro: <sheet InstanceContent $n1 3> — a value from a game data sheet, such as a name; sheet = InstanceContent, row = number parameter 1, column = 3 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <if ($n3 == 1)><if $n3><if ($n3 <= 10)><switch $n3><case>one<case>two<case>three<case>four<case>five<case>six<case>seven<case>eight<case>nine<case>ten</switch><… — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = number parameter 3 == 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
